@startuml
title Login Flow with Two-Layer Authentication

actor User
participant Browser
participant "Crypto Module" as Crypto
participant "Local Storage\n(IndexedDB)" as LS
participant Server
database Database

== Account Login (Traditional) ==
User -> Browser: Login (username + password)
Browser -> Server: POST /auth/login
Server -> Database: verify credentials
Server -> Browser: account session token

== Crypto Key Loading ==
alt Local-only key mode
  Browser -> LS: loadEncryptedPrivateKey()
else Cloud-backed key mode
  Browser -> Server: GET /auth/crypto/fetch-backup\n(requires account session)
  Server -> Database: retrieveEncryptedKey()
  Server -> Browser: encryptedPrivateKey
end

User -> Browser: Enter key passphrase
Browser -> Crypto: decryptPrivateKey(passphrase)

alt Passphrase correct
  Crypto -> Browser: privateKey in memory
else Passphrase incorrect
  Crypto -> Browser: decryption failed
  Browser -> User: passphrase error
end

== Crypto Authentication (Challenge-Response) ==
Browser -> Server: POST /auth/crypto/challenge\n(requires account session)
Server -> Browser: cryptographic challenge
Browser -> Crypto: sign(challenge)
Browser -> Server: POST /auth/crypto/verify\n(signature + account session)
Server -> Browser: crypto authentication success

opt After inactivity timeout (15 min)
  Browser -> Crypto: wipePrivateKeyFromMemory()
end

note right of Browser
Two security layers:
1. Account access (password)
2. Crypto operations (private key)
end note

@enduml
